# Resolve packages from the public registry, whatever a machine's global npmrc says.
#
# package-lock.json records an absolute `resolved` URL per package, so a lockfile
# generated behind a private mirror pins every tarball to a host that only exists
# on that network. GitHub's runners then sit on `npm ci` until npm gives up
# ("Exit handler never called!"), which is what broke the Pages deploy.
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
